# Session close (SITE 00 — required every time)

**Founder formalized this rule so they never type it again.** Do not suggest the founder add session-close text to sprint prompts. This file is always-applied — compliance is mandatory, not optional.

Founder works from **mobile**. Every agent turn that **completes work**, **wraps a sprint**, or **merges a PR** MUST end with **all three parts below**. Missing any part is a failed close — do not send prose-only.

## The three parts (in order)

### 1. Text summary (prose)
Normal markdown: what changed, why, what founder does next (Railway redeploy, Supabase migration, etc.).

### 2. Structured conclusion code box (copy-paste BLOCK)
One fenced code block for founder mobile copy-paste.

- If the user/sprint provided a `CONCLUSION` or `FINAL CONCLUSION FORMAT` template, paste that template **filled in** inside this box.
- If no sprint template, use a short STATUS block ending with `STOP.`
- **Do NOT put deploy URLs inside this box.**

### 3. Deploy links (each on its own line)
Immediately after the code box — bare URLs or markdown links, **one per line** (founder copies one at a time on mobile):

1. Direct ZIP download URL
2. GitHub Release page URL
3. SITE00-DEPLOY-README.txt download URL (if release exists)
4. One-line verify reminder (e.g. must NOT reference `index.BT7zuSxb.js`)
5. One-line upload reminder (GoDaddy public_html → upload → extract → hard refresh)

## When frontend or UI changed

Before closing you MUST:

1. Run `bash scripts/package-cpanel-deploy.sh`
2. Create a new GitHub Release (`site00-deploy-YYYY-MM-DD-vN`) with the ZIP + README
3. Include fresh download links in part 3

API-only changes still require part 1 + 2; part 3 deploy links required if any `src/` or UI bundle changed in the session.

## Common failures (do not repeat)

- Sprint prompt has its own CONCLUSION template → agent delivers that in **prose markdown** instead of a **code box**
- Agent merges PR and stops — treats git shipping as "done" without session close
- Deploy reminder buried in prose with no ZIP link
- All links bundled inside one code box (founder cannot copy one at a time)
- Conversation handoff/summary drops close-format requirement — **re-read this rule before final message**

## Checklist before sending final message

- [ ] Part 1 prose summary present
- [ ] Part 2 conclusion in a single fenced code block (not markdown headings)
- [ ] Part 3 deploy links each on separate line (if UI changed)
- [ ] Fresh ZIP release built if frontend changed this session
